  "status_text": "A hundred lights can go out together and count as one drop when working out how many gates must flip bits. Lean checked this when input bits turn on one at a time in a fixed order and all lights are prescribed at those steps. Let c count steps when at least one light goes out. With AND, OR and NOT gates reading at most two wires and two free constants, the minimum number b of NOTs is the smallest with 2^b > c. One circuit attains it with at most 4c+2R other gates, where R counts maximal lit stretches separately for each light and adds them up (L-lib-1286).",
